msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Examples.rst:176
msgid "Second, calculate the head loss but assume that the upflow velocity is negligible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Examples.rst:178
msgid ":math:`h_e = \\frac{\\ {\\bar v_{diff}}^2}{2g}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Examples.rst:180
msgid "`Is it reasonable to neglect the upflow velocity in the clarifier when calculating this head loss? <https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1lE7cHu3TS1vMs0_yA3FmNdPnk3iktBJw#scrollTo=mT6cY0pGbzKt&line=1&uniqifier=1>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Examples.rst:182
msgid "**Answer:** The best estimate of the exit head loss for the diffuser is 0.6176 centimeter. The 2nd estimate of the exit head loss for the diffuser ignoring the upflow velocity is 0.6211 centimeter. It is reasonable to neglect the effect of the upflow velocity. The error is 0.005755 dimensionless"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Examples.rst:185
msgid "Manifolds and Launders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Examples.rst:186
msgid "Flow distribution between and within clarifiers is an important design component to ensure good clarifier performance. We need to distribute flow uniformly between clarifiers and also between diffusers on the inlet manifolds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Examples.rst:188
msgid "The following variable definitions and equations will be useful in answering later questions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Examples.rst:190
msgid "Determine the relationship between diffuser exit velocity and the head loss in the parallel paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Examples.rst:192
msgid ":math:`{h}_{L,ParallelPath}` is the head loss (flow resistance) in the parallel paths leaving the manifold. The head loss in the parallel path is the total head loss from where the flow leaves the manifold to the point where the parallel flows reunite."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Examples.rst:194
msgid ":math:`\\Delta{H}_{Manifold}` is the variability in piezometric head in the manifold that is driving the flow through the parallel paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Examples.rst:196
msgid "The ratio of minimum (first diffuser port) to maximum (last diffuser port) flow is given by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Examples.rst:198
msgid "\\Pi_{DiffuserFlow} = \\sqrt{\\frac{h_{L,parallelpath} - \\frac{\\Delta{H}_{Manifold}}{2}}{h_{L,parallelpath} + \\frac{\\Delta{H}_{Manifold}}{2}}}\n"
"\n"
""
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Examples.rst:200
msgid "The change in piezometric head is given by: :math:`\\Delta{H}_{Manifold} = \\frac{{v_{manifold}}^{2}}{2g}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Examples.rst:202
msgid "The maximum allowable velocity in the manifold is given by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Examples.rst:204
msgid "{\\Pi_{DiffuserFlow}}^{2} * \\left(h_{L,parallelpath} + \\frac{\\Delta{H}_{Manifold}}{2} \\right) = h_{L,parallelpath} - \\frac{\\Delta{H}_{Manifold}}{2}\n"
"\n"
""
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Examples.rst:206
msgid "\\left({\\Pi_{DiffuserFlow}}^{2} - 1 \\right) h_{L,parallelpath} + \\left({\\Pi{DiffuserFlow}}^{2} + 1 \\right) \\frac{\\Delta{H}_{Manifold}}{2} = 0\n"
"\n"
""
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Examples.rst:208
msgid "\\left(\\frac{1 - {\\Pi_{DiffuserFlow}}^{2}}{{\\Pi_{DiffuserFlow}}^{2} + 1} \\right) h_{L,parallelpath} = \\frac{\\Delta{H}_{Manifold}}{2}\n"
"\n"
""
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Examples.rst:210
msgid "\\left(\\frac{1 - {\\Pi_{DiffuserFlow}}^{2}}{{\\Pi_{DiffuserFlow}}^{2} + 1} \\right) h_{L,parallelpath} = \\frac{{v_{manifold}}^{2}}{4g}\n"
"\n"
""
msgstr ""

